---
id: org.dxos.plugin.autocue
name: AutocuePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A plugin for `DXOS` Composer that plays autocue demo bundles: recorded walkthroughs of the app with their steps as
chapters, the `.mdl` test they were recorded from, where they were recorded, and a prompt to record them again. A
bundle is made by the `autocue` skill (`pack.mjs --upload`) and hosted on dx.pub; this plugin links one into a space
and plays it with the `@dxos/autocue/player` Player. Recording stays in the skill (phase 2 of
`tools/autocue/DESIGN.md` moves it behind a loopback service the plugin can call).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`    |

## Types

```mdl
type AutocueBundle
  desc: A link to an autocue bundle (`org.dxos.type.autocueBundle@0.1.0`).
  fields:
    name?: string
    url?: string    # the bundle folder, its index.html, or its autocue.json

type Manifest
  desc: The bundle's `autocue.json` (`autocue@1`), from `@dxos/autocue/player`; specified in
    `.agents/skills/autocue/FORMAT.md`.
```

## Components

```mdl
component BundlePlayer
  desc: Fetches the bundle's manifest with `loadBundle`, rebases its paths onto the bundle's URL, and plays it with
    the Player in `embedded` layout (fills its container; keys only while focus is inside).
  props:
    url?: string
  state:
    status: loading | ready | error

component AutocueArticle
  desc: The article surface for an AutocueBundle; a Panel around BundlePlayer.
  props:
    subject: AutocueBundle
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Link a bundle
  req F-1.1: The create-object menu offers a Demo (AutocueBundle) with a name and URL.

feat F-2: Play a bundle
  req F-2.1: The article fetches `<url>/autocue.json` and plays the bundle's demos, chapters, spec, recording and prompt.
  req F-2.2: Bundle-relative video, poster and archive paths resolve against the bundle's URL, not the app's.
  req F-2.3: The player's keys act only while focus is inside the article.
  req F-2.4: A missing URL, an unreachable host or a non-autocue response shows a message instead of the player.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Play a hosted bundle
  given: an AutocueBundle whose url is a dx.pub bundle
  then: the article shows the first demo's video with its chapters in the side panel

scenario T-2: Bad URL
  given: an AutocueBundle whose url answers 404
  then: the article says the bundle could not be loaded and names the URL
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Link a demo bundle and play it
  desc: The core round-trip — create a Demo pointing at a hosted bundle, play it, and step through its chapters.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3]
  status: blocked            # 2026-11-01, passes end to end by autocue/qa-1.mjs with #14348's app-graph change reverted
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-autocue is enabled — it is a labs plugin, default-on only under `isDev`
    - url: a hosted autocue bundle whose host allows the app's origin (dx.pub does)
    - no Demo named "QA Demo" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the demo
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Demo. Name it "QA Demo" and set its URL to `$given.url`.
      capture: created
      expect: a Demo named "QA Demo" appears under the collection and its article opens
      note: NO `invoke` — there is no create operation, only the navtree factory (`capabilities/create-object.ts`).
        On main at caa28b313a7 (app-graph #14348) a newly created object of any type opens as a "Loading…" plank
        that never resolves; reverting that commit's AppGraph.ts and util.ts changes fixes it.
    - name: Play it
      do: Click the play button over the video.
      expect: the video plays and the first chapter is highlighted in the Chapters panel
    - name: Step through the chapters
      do: Click inside the article, then press → twice.
      expect: the playhead jumps to the third chapter and the Chapters panel highlights it
    - name: Keys stay in the article
      do: Click the navtree, then press →.
      expect: the playhead does not move
  after:
    - name: Delete the demo
      do: Right-click "QA Demo" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: A new private plugin-autocue hosts the Player, not plugin-video
  date: 2026-11-01
  by: user:burdon
  why: a bundle (several demos, chapters, spec, prompt) is a different object from plugin-video's Video, and a
    separate plugin keeps both small.

decision D-2: The Player keeps @dxos/plugin-deck's Pane for its chrome
  date: 2026-11-01
  by: user:burdon
  why: rebuilding the plank chrome from react-ui primitives would change the player's look; the dependency is noted
    in tools/autocue/DESIGN.md for a later pass.

decision D-3: QA-1 is blocked on main by the app-graph regression, not by this plugin
  date: 2026-11-01
  by: agent:claude-opus-5-5
  why: with caa28b313a7 (#14348) in place no newly created object opens (Video too); with its AppGraph.ts and
    util.ts changes reverted, autocue/qa-1.mjs passes all five steps (take at
    https://dx.pub/demo/2026-11-01-plugin-autocue-qa-1/).
```
